  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscComm 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'A research team is exploring new ideas for cancer treatments in the
    lab and is unsure how to best explain this early work to the community. They
    ask your organization what information matters most and what would help build
    trust.

    

    <b>In this situation, what impact do community advocates
    have on research and the community?</b>'
  explanation: "Community advocates help scientists share research in ways that patients
    and families can easily understand. By sharing their perspective, advocates help
    shape how research is explained, encourage transparency, and build trust between
    the research team and the community. Their feedback ensures that research is
    clear, meaningful, and connected to the needs and perspectives of the cancer
    patient community\u2014even at the earliest stages of discovery."
  correctAnswer: They help shape how researchers communicate and build trust with
    the community
  incorrectAnswer1: They help decide which lab experiments the research team should
    run next
  incorrectAnswer2: They review the data and approve the study so the research can
    move forward
  incorrectAnswer3: They help manage the scientific data collected in the lab during
    early discovery
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
